# --- Secrets & data ---
# NOTE: /data/ is anchored to the repo root so it only ignores the engine's OUTPUT
# directory, NOT the engine/ai_investing/data/ source package.
# Every .env variant, not just two names. `.env.before-live` — a full copy of
# the file including broker tokens — sat untracked and UNIGNORED on the trading
# box on 2026-08-04, one `git add -A` away from being published. Allow-list the
# example instead of trying to enumerate the backups people will make.
.env*
!.env.example
# `/data/*` rather than `/data/`: git does not descend into an ignored
# DIRECTORY, so a negation for a file inside one can never take effect. Listing
# the children is what makes the single exception below reachable. Everything
# under data/ stays ignored either way.
/data/*
*.db
*.sqlite
*.log
/data/state.json
# ...except the curated drop-directory's own instructions. That file is
# documentation, not state, and shipping it is what CREATES the directory on a
# deploy — a door nobody can find is not a door. Nothing else under
# data/curated/ is tracked: the research dropped there is the operator's, may
# be paywalled or private, and has no business in a git history (see the .env
# note above for how that goes).
!/data/curated/
/data/curated/*
!/data/curated/README.md

